  <static seed="2105" source="Contrib/PCC/BasicMath/FractionPercentDecimal/DecimalToFraction30.pg">
    <statement><p>Write the decimal number as a fraction.</p>
<p><m>0.15</m> = <fillin characters="11" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>{\frac{3}{20}}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p><m>0.15</m> is read as fifteen hundredth, so it can be written as <m>\frac{15}{100}</m>, which can be reduced to <m>{{\frac{3}{20}}}</m> by dividing <m>5</m> in both the numerator and denominator.</p>
</solution>
